+## Target A seed 66: coembedded locked stress with full Schur rank (2026-10-13)
+
+Run `python3 -I -O -B research/verify_target_a_seed066_locked_fullrank.py`.
+The [unreviewed proof report](../docs/reports/target_a_seed066_coembedded_locked_fullrank_2026-10-13.md)
+constructs a family that is maximum in its own hexagonal hull and locally isolated
+there, with positive contact/facet stress, full Schur column rank for every nonzero
+edge weighting, and a three-spoke locked fan with exactly one crossing response row.
+The script uses integer axial coordinates and exact `Fraction` arithmetic. At
+`m=2,3,4,8` it checks every source pair, all label equilibrium equations, the entire
+response shore, exact Schur elimination, and every fan/response crossing. Integer
+pinned rigidity is certified full rank modulo a prime at `m=2,3,4`. At `m=32` it
+constructs a 3,169-point strict-diameter replacement and checks all 5,019,696 pairs.
+Six negative controls must fail. The deterministic output is preserved in
+`target_a_seed066_locked_fullrank_certificate.json`.
+
+These finite checks support the report's analytic all-`m` regression, not its
+promotion or an infinite computational proof. The family is nonglobal for `m>=32`,
+contains triangles, and supplies no canonical triangle-free source/collar coupling.
+The construction falsifies a stress/container/affine-optimality shortcut to positive
+Schur nullity; it does not refute Sections 175–177 or settle Level I. No new claim is
+registered as canonical, and no theorem-state version or active route is changed.

