+## Seed 54: finite endpoints and rhombus-mesh growth (2026-10-13)
+
+Run `python3 research/verify_seed054_rhombus_mesh.py` and compare its JSON
+with `research/seed054_rhombus_mesh_certificate.json`; then run
+`python3 research/check_seed054_cartesian_certificate.py`. The primary engine
+generates complete connected unit-rhombus meshes with one off-lattice contact
+isolate, checks every possible source lattice displacement, every isolate
+pair, exact hull diameters, triangle-freeness, equal-cardinality triangular
+replacements, and the local length-growth counts in their actual endpoint
+labelings. The separate Cartesian engine independently generates vertices,
+uses a different hull algorithm, and directly enumerates every source and
+replacement pair in the 1893- and 5259-label fixtures. The 13141- and
+66657-label fixtures use the proved integral norm classification and hull
+extremality; quadratic enumeration of their larger ledgers is not claimed.
+Both engines use only integer and rational arithmetic and include the isolate
+in the full source/replacement counts. Positive output certifies these four
+finite nonglobal fixtures and their strict replacements. It does not prove
+the infinite endpoint rigidity, the at-least-ceil(R/8) cell-growth theorem,
+global optimality, canonical source extraction, or Level I. The first two
+are proved analytically, as unreviewed candidates, in
+`docs/reports/global_nonexpanding_rhombus_mesh_obstruction_2026-10-13.md`.
+The exact endpoint theorem needs no continuous feasible interpolation. The
+linear growth bound requires endpoint diameter at most 2(R-1); it is not
+asserted for every arbitrarily small strict improvement. No new certificate
+is registered as canonical.

